/target

# Everything this program writes into whatever directory it is run from.
#
# A snapshot carries an account's name and every game it owns; the opener script carries the
# pages somebody picked. Both are personal, this repository is meant to be published, and one
# `git add -A` is all it takes — so the rule is that anything written into a working directory
# gets its entry here in the same change that starts writing it.
/game_lib_*
/game_wishlist_*
/catalogames-open.sh

# Checkouts of other projects, kept beside this one while they are iterated on together — a
# dependency, or another program that shares one. Each is its OWN git repository, so `git add -A`
# here would not add its files: it would add a gitlink naming a commit that exists only in this
# checkout, and no .gitmodules to say where to find it. Anyone cloning would get a directory git
# calls a submodule and cannot fill.
/terminal_choice/
/os_ricing/
